# Runner scenarios (plan 04-20, D-20, D-21, D-23): `<id> <exit> <outcome> <class> <skip>
# <operator-args>`, six fixed columns, the first token the id. Each id names
# data/scenarios/<id>.ivss; suite runner-process (tests/runner-process-tap.sh) runs every line
# through the real ivs-run and requires the exit code and outcome given here.
#   class          deterministic, or host-dependent (wall time, signals): the golden step of plan
#                  04-21 excludes host-dependent reports from the dev versus release comparison
#                  and refuses goldens for them (D-21: the wall watchdog is never golden).
#   skip           run, skip-ok, or release-only. skip-ok: the scenario needs operator content the gate
#                  never has; it is judged like any other and a passing judgement is a visible skip.
#                  release-only (plan 09-01, D-09, A-03): the scenario runs on the Release preset only and is
#                  judged statically on the sanitized Debug preset by the derivation equality of
#                  docs/video/demo-lamp-tone-1-derivation.md; it prints an ordinary ok line on both presets,
#                  never a skip, and tests-skipped does not move.
#   operator-args  extra ivs-run words joined by `,`, or `-` for none.
# One demonstrating scenario per outcome (D-20): pass 0, guest-fail 10, timeout 11, cancelled 12,
# missing-fixture 13, harness-fail 14.
diag-boot-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
guest-assert-mismatch 10 guest-fail deterministic run -
timeout-budget 11 timeout deterministic run -
timeout-wall 11 timeout host-dependent run --wall-timeout-ms,1,--slice-ticks,4
cancel-signal 12 cancelled host-dependent run --self-signal-after-slices,1,--slice-ticks,4
missing-cart-file 13 missing-fixture deterministic run -
needs-user-exec 13 missing-fixture deterministic skip-ok -
bad-syntax 14 harness-fail deterministic run -
unexpected-refusal 14 harness-fail deterministic run -
expect-load-refusal 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-input-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
max-ticks-straddle 0 pass deterministic run --max-ticks,99
dead-after-refusal 14 harness-fail deterministic run -
no-run-to 14 harness-fail deterministic run -
cancel-signal-twice 12 cancelled host-dependent run --self-signal-after-slices,1,--self-signal-count,2,--slice-ticks,4
psg-log-assert-mismatch 10 guest-fail deterministic run -
diag-ctrl-psg-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-ctrl-psg-nokey 11 timeout deterministic run -
diag-ctrl-psg-order 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic-fgbg-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic-cstack-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
video-assert-mismatch 10 guest-fail deterministic run -
demo-lamp-tone-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
demo-lamp-tone-idle 0 pass deterministic run -
demo-lamp-tone-shift 0 pass deterministic release-only -
demo-lamp-tone-swap 0 pass deterministic release-only -
diag-stic2-idle-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic2-mob-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic2-border-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic2-hdelay-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic2-vdelay-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
diag-stic2-collision-pass 0 pass deterministic run -
bench-lamp-idle 0 pass deterministic run -
bench-lamp-input 0 pass deterministic run -
owner-exec-title 13 missing-fixture deterministic skip-ok -
# Plan 19-02 (VID-07, criterion 5): the owner-local sweep probe tools/disc-sweep.sh has no case of its own in the gate, because its input is
# the operator's own EXEC image and the gate never has one (D11). This row is its visible skip marker, beside the two skip-ok rows above: the
# scenario asks for `content exec user`, so the gate ends it missing-fixture with exit 13, the suite judges it like any other and reports the
# passing judgement as a skip, and the probe's absence is the expected state rather than a gap. The scenario names no cartridge on purpose
# (data/scenarios/disc-sweep-probe.ivss says why): a loadable program would destroy the declared outcome.
disc-sweep-probe 13 missing-fixture deterministic skip-ok -
